        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.74,
            0.385,
            0.759
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pause and Ponder"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.77,
            0.906,
            0.816
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. A compound consists of 40% sulfur and 60% oxygen by mass. In a sample of the same compound containing 20 g of sulfur, what mass of oxygen must be present to satisfy the Law of Constant Proportions?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.816,
            0.905,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. Carbon monoxide (CO) contains carbon and oxygen in the mass ratio of 3:4. How much oxygen will combine with 9 g of carbon to form carbon monoxide?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.846,
            0.905,
            0.862
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. The Law of Definite Proportions holds true for compounds but not for mixtures. Give reason."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.139,
            0.861,
            0.906,
            0.908
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. Students X and Y, both prepared an oxide of copper by combining copper and oxygen in the ratios of 4:1 and 8:2, respectively. Do their results justify the Law of Constant Proportions? Explain."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
